`BIDSDataset` no longer lets subject metadata replace the coordinates it reads from the files (`obs`, `epoch`, `recording_id`, `bad_channels`, `subject`, `session`, `run`). A `subject_metadata_df` keyed on a column named `subject` replaced the `subject` coordinate with the table's own labels (`sub-01` instead of `01`), and any `participants.tsv` or metadata column with one of these names did the same. The `subject_key` column now only matches rows to subjects and is not attached; another column with such a name raises an error asking to rename it.
